CHAPTER.VERS:
therefore you will with all diligence buy with this money bullocks, rams, lambs, with their meal-offerings and their drink-offerings, and will offer them on the altar of the house of your

          {+}
         God which is in Jerusalem.

And whatever will seem good to you and to your brothers to do with the rest of the silver and the gold, do

          {+}
         that after the will of your

          {+}
         God.

And I, even I Artaxerxes the king, make a decree to all the treasurers who are beyond the River, that whatever Ezra the priest, the scribe of the law of the God of heaven, will require of you

          {+}
        , it is to be done with all diligence,

Also we inform you

          {+}
        , that concerning any of the priests and Levites, the singers, porters, Nethinim, or servants of this house of God, it will not be lawful to impose tribute, custom, or toll, on them.

And you, Ezra, after the wisdom of your God that is in your hand, appoint magistrates and judges, who may judge all the people who are beyond the River, all such as know the laws of your God; and teach

          {+}
         him who doesn't know them.
